# Lore drafts (canon: soft): minor figures and families.

@lore vaneshade
keys: Vaneshade, Lady Vaneshade, black seal, winter gala
canon: soft
text: House Vaneshade is old pyromancer nobility. Its letters carry a black seal; its winter gala is an inspection disguised as a party; its duellists carry pale family wands and open every duel with the same flame flourish they have used for two hundred years. Vaneshades sleep exactly eight hours. Lady Vaneshade's highest praise is "Adequate"; she has a velvet chair reserved at her daughter's bouts, and it stays empty.

@lore oracle_of_vell
keys: Oracle of Vell, Vell, family seat
canon: soft
text: The Oracle of Vell, Seraphine's mother, tells kings what they want to hear and has already seen her daughter say yes to taking the family seat.

@lore fennick_farm
keys: Fennick, farm, harvest, blight, turnip scholarship, scholarship board
canon: soft
text: The Fennick farm grows turnips, tomatoes and stubborn children. Tobias's mother runs it alone at harvest, writes weather first and love last, and expects him home after graduation; one year blight nearly ruined them. Tobias studies on an agricultural scholarship whose board reviews his marks in person.

@lore ten_clockworks
keys: Ten family, clockworks, guild medal, name day
canon: soft
text: Mir's family runs a clockworks, calls invention a hobby and expects Mir home. After a persuasive letter, Mir's mother agreed: "Fine. Win a prize": the guild medal for young artificers. The family keeps name days, not birthdays; Mir's father shows almost nobody the escapement of his clocks.

@lore ashby_family
keys: Ashby, Corvin's brother, Corvin's grandfather
canon: soft
text: Corvin's grandfather could find a lost thing in any house, taught Corvin to shuffle on rainy Sundays, and owned a genuinely lucky deck of cards that later sat in the confiscation vault. Corvin's brother turns up at the gates wanting money. Home, Corvin says, is not a good place.

@lore hollis_family
keys: Hollis, Bram's father, head boy, head boys' portraits
canon: soft
text: Bram's father was a prefect and head boy at Lumenhold; his portrait hangs in the corridor of head boys, and he stops in front of it on every visit. He has never stopped telling his son he will not amount to anything.

@lore grisk
keys: Grisk, goblin, moneylender, debt
canon: soft
text: A goblin in a velvet waistcoat, friend to the temporarily embarrassed: sixty crowns today, twelve a month for six months. He keeps a ledger and occasionally asks for favours instead of coin.

@lore prudence_ashworth
keys: Prudence Ashworth, ghost, socks
canon: soft
text: A polite ghost from two hundred years ago who rearranges socks to get attention. She was in love with the baker's daughter and never delivered her letter.

@lore footnote
keys: Footnote, library cat
canon: soft
text: The library cat, who sleeps on the reference desk and decides which books are worth reading.

@lore bartholomew
keys: Bartholomew, goat
canon: soft
text: Maud's goat, who has eaten parts of the Restricted Section and most of a sleeve. He likes some students more than others.

@lore gerald
keys: Gerald, mandrake
canon: soft
text: Tobias's mandrake, who wears a knitted hat, screams softly and bites the people he loves.

@lore ember_fox
keys: Ember, fox, ember tail
canon: soft
text: A small fox with a tail that smoulders like an ember. If you free her from a snare she may come back with a ruby, or stay.

@lore pim
keys: Pim, first-year, mentee
canon: soft
text: A nervous first-year who attaches to final-year students in need of a mentor.

@lore duchess_of_ambry
keys: Duchess of Ambry, portrait
canon: soft
text: An escaped portrait who wanders the castle's frames, gossiping and refusing to return to her own.

@lore professors
keys: Professor Marisol, Professor Vey, Professor Brask
canon: soft
text: Professor Marisol teaches Tidecalling and keeps the lake calm on exam days. Professor Vey teaches Illusion and grades on whether you fooled her. Professor Brask teaches Beastcraft and is kinder to animals than to students.

@lore clockwork_owl
keys: clockwork owl, brass owl
canon: soft
text: Mir's brass owl with amber eyes: it hoots the hour, remembers deadlines and birthdays, and refuses to work for Professor Thorne.

@lore thornes_rival
keys: wizard in purple, rematch
canon: soft
text: A flamboyant old wizard in purple who has wanted to settle a forty-year-old matter with Thorne. The rematch lasts four seconds; afterwards both old men laugh until they wheeze.

@lore isolde_youth
keys: young headmistress, portrait, observatory fire
canon: soft
text: Before she was headmistress, Isolde Marrow was the student with the detention record of the decade, who set the observatory on fire twice.

@lore tamsin_reed
keys: Tamsin Reed, Tamsin, pen pal
canon: soft
text: A Thornwick illusionist in the player's year, a pen pal since their first term. Raised in a travelling theatre; sly in letters, loyal in person. Thornwick set them to spy on Lumenhold through their letters, and they gave it up for the friendship.

@lore odile_varn
keys: Odile Varn, Odile, the fourth-year's notebook
canon: soft
text: A fourth-year in Umbral Theory, graduating, who kept a notebook on the Restricted Section in three colours of ink and passed it on, with a silver key to its door, to a student she thought would use it. What she read there frightened her into finishing early.
